(1778764887, 1778326397, '1', 'MOMOREMIT FIXES REQUIRED [SPECIFICALLY CASHIN MERCHANT]\r\nIf transaction is Cashing, and category is sending, sim type is merchant\r\nCharging type: Charge is amount deducted from amount to send. It is a charge applied on merchant sims during cashin sending (0.5% of amount to send). \r\nIf charging type is â€˜+ feeâ€™: the charge is added to the amount payable. The amount deducted from the userâ€™s ecash channel of the cashdrawer is equal to amount to send plus the 0.5% of the amount to send. \r\nIf charging type is â€˜- feeâ€™, the amount is deducted from the amount to send. The amount to be deducted from users ecash channel of the cashdrawer. = amount to send + 0.5% of amount to send. \r\nSending type: This is made of in fee (1% of amount involved) and out fee (0.5% of amount involved). The in fee is recorded as commission. The out fee is added to amount payable and amount to send if it is available. The in fee is always applied if transaction type is sending but based on the sending type, it may be added to amount payable or subtracted from amount to send. But it is always recorded as commission. There are three types of sending: Only in, Subtract in and In/out\r\nIf only in: 1% of amount involved is added to amount payable. This does not reduce the amount to send but increases amount payable\r\nIf subtract in: 1% of amount involved is subtracted from the amount involved. This reduces the amount to send but does not affect amount payable\r\nIf in/out: 1% of amount involved is added to amount payable (this is the in fee). The in fee increases amount payable and does not affect amount to send. The out fee is  0.5% of amount involved. It is and added to amount payable and amount to send. This affects both amount payable and amount to send.\r\nTotal charge system calculated = sending fee (in fee + out fee if available) + charge applied (0.5% of amount to send)\r\nCASE I: If charging type is + fee and sending type is Subtract in:\r\nEXAMPLE:\r\nIf amount involved =4000\r\nIn fee = 4000 * 1% = 40 (also recorded as commission)\r\nAmount to send = 4000 - 40 = 3960\r\nCharge applied = 3960 * 0.5% = 19.80\r\nTotal charge [system calculated] = 40 + 19.80 = 59.80\r\nAmount payable = 4000 + 19.8 = 4019.80\r\nAmount to be deducted from users ecash channel = 3960 + 19.8 = 3979.80\r\nCASE II: If charging type is + fee and sending type is in/out (in and out):\r\nEXAMPLE:\r\nIf amount involved =4000\r\nIn fee = 4000 * 1% = 40 (also recorded as commission)\r\nOut fee = 4000 * 0.5% = 20\r\nAmount to send = 4000 + 20 = 4020\r\nCharge applied = 4020 * 0.5% = 20.10\r\nTotal charge [system calculated] = 40 + 20 + 20.10 = 80.10\r\nAmount payable = 4000 + 40 + 20 + 20.1 = 4080.10\r\nAmount to be deducted from users ecash channel = 4000 + 20 + 20.10 = 4040.10\r\nCASE III: If charging type is + fee and sending type is only in:\r\nEXAMPLE:\r\nIf amount involved =4000\r\nIn fee = 4000 * 1% = 40 (also recorded as commission)\r\nAmount to send = 4000\r\nCharge applied = 4000 * 0.5% = 20\r\nTotal charge [system calculated] = 40 + 20 = 60\r\nAmount payable = 4000 + 40 + 20 = 4060\r\nAmount to be deducted from users ecash channel = 4000 + 20  = 4020\r\nCASE IV: If charging type is â€˜- feeâ€™ and sending type is â€˜subtract inâ€™:\r\nEXAMPLE:\r\nIf amount involved =4000\r\nIn fee = 4000 * 1% = 40 (also recorded as commission)\r\nCharge applied = (4000 - 40) * 0.5% = 19.8\r\nAmount to send = 4000 - 40 - 19.80 = 3940.20 \r\nTotal charge [system calculated] = 40 + 19.8 = 59.80\r\nAmount payable = 4000\r\nAmount to be deducted from users ecash channel = 3940.20 + 19.80 = 3960\r\nCASE V: If charging type is â€˜- feeâ€™ and sending type is â€˜in/outâ€™:\r\nEXAMPLE:\r\nIf amount involved =4000\r\nIn fee = 4000 * 1% = 40 (also recorded as commission)\r\nOut fee = 4000 * 0.5% = 20\r\nAmount payable = 4000 + 40 + 20 = 4060\r\nCharge applied = (4000 + 20) * 0.5% = 20.10\r\nAmount to send = 4000 + 20 - 20.10 = 3999.90\r\nTotal charge [system calculated] = 40 + 20 + 20.10 = 80.10\r\nAmount to be deducted from users ecash channel = 3999.90 + 20.10 = 4020\r\nCASE V: If charging type is â€˜- feeâ€™ and sending type is â€˜only inâ€™:\r\nEXAMPLE:\r\nIf amount involved =4000\r\nIn fee = 4000 * 1% = 40 (also recorded as commission)\r\nAmount payable = 4000 + 40 = 4040\r\nCharge applied = 4000 * 0.5% = 20\r\nAmount to send = 4000 - 20 = 3980\r\nTotal charge [system calculated] = 40 + 20  = 60\r\nAmount to be deducted from users ecash channel = 3980 + 20 = 4000\r\n', NULL, 0, '1', '2026-05-14 13:21:27'),
